{% comment %}
  Renders a customer-facing brand line for a product.

  VennixStore imports products from fulfilment partners, so `product.vendor` can hold a
  supplier name (for example a dropship partner) rather than the brand the customer is
  buying from. This snippet is the single presentation-layer gate for vendor output:
  the underlying Shopify vendor data is never modified, it is simply not shown to
  customers while `settings.hide_supplier_vendor` is enabled.

  Behaviour:
  - `settings.hide_supplier_vendor` on  -> renders `settings.storefront_brand_name`
    (falling back to `shop.name`) when the product's vendor is NOT already that brand,
    and renders the vendor untouched when it already matches the brand.
  - `settings.hide_supplier_vendor` off -> renders `product.vendor` as-is.
  - Renders nothing when there is nothing safe to show.

  Accepts:
  - product: {Object} Product Liquid object (required)
  - fallback_to_brand: {Boolean} When false, renders nothing instead of substituting the
    brand name for a supplier vendor. Default: true (optional)

  Usage:
  {%- render 'vennix-vendor', product: card_product -%}
  {%- capture vendor_name -%}{%- render 'vennix-vendor', product: product -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign vx_vendor = product.vendor | strip
  assign vx_brand = settings.storefront_brand_name | default: shop.name | strip
  assign vendor_compare = vx_vendor | downcase
  assign brand_compare = vx_brand | downcase

  if settings.hide_supplier_vendor == false or vendor_compare == brand_compare
    echo vx_vendor
  elsif fallback_to_brand != false
    echo vx_brand
  endif
-%}
